#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7693381a-adc8-583e-94af-eadf35214759" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}={x}^{2}-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349353} {:answer/id #uuid "80928768-2894-5d85-acfd-cfd9ea38e5e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2y}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349354} {:answer/id #uuid "f04e9899-6b36-5518-85d3-c461808ed265" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349355} {:answer/id #uuid "ad191047-c971-55bb-8128-f0ada4a095ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2y}={x}^{2}-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349356} {:answer/id #uuid "bf9a5b8d-2843-51eb-8e6f-76f48f63f4fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7693381a-adc8-583e-94af-eadf35214759" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}={x}^{2}-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349353} :answer-field/id #uuid "12dab8f4-e734-5963-9693-5c1406154eb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3385e109-e3cb-5f6a-8feb-75ceb2f55ae4" :question/math-academy-id "q-154369" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{-y}(x-1).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2{e}^{-y}(x-1) \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x & =\\int 2(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{2}-2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{e}^{y}={x}^{2}-2x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e56dec5-b70f-5cf7-9d7d-32891777a0de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-1/x}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349360} {:answer/id #uuid "2d125910-295e-59ed-8a6a-e393f3053a49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{x}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349361} {:answer/id #uuid "eb037adf-0cb2-5567-a884-d4e68c98b5fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{1/x}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349362} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9dbab8-ae4f-56e6-8695-b2f20aead6a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-x}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349363} {:answer/id #uuid "9000bafb-6ff6-58fe-8e85-0ad592433b87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-3/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e56dec5-b70f-5cf7-9d7d-32891777a0de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-1/x}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349360} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3c1a1ea-775c-5824-ada6-11750b012916" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349359}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "699032fa-9b2d-5062-8641-470288705407" :question/math-academy-id "q-158009" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${x}^{2}\\,{y}^{′}-y=3$ for $y\\ne -3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\,{y}^{′}-y & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y+3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y+3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y+3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y+3}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y+3| & =-\\frac{1}{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y+3|=-\\frac{1}{x}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y+3| & =-\\frac{1}{x}+C \\\\ |y+3| & ={e}^{-1/x+C} \\\\ |y+3| & ={e}^{-1/x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y+3| & =K{e}^{-1/x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|y+3| & =K{e}^{-1/x} \\\\ y+3 & =K{e}^{-1/x} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{-1/x}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc369823-8d5e-5fb4-9843-2b1db974b760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290036} {:answer/id #uuid "c9faa650-8742-503d-9056-30ec4f094de3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(\\sqrt[3]{x}+C)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290037} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2de853-237e-5dd0-a350-1dc2b509ce7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{2x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290038} {:answer/id #uuid "79e4646a-be4c-528c-835d-efc1f7784fef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290039} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb6361a-1bcc-517b-bdc8-ffd88e20b18e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{3}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc369823-8d5e-5fb4-9843-2b1db974b760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290036} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e81955a-cb56-51ae-900b-0a206645fb7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84edc4b8-8df5-5463-b957-9bbf44dd553d" :question/math-academy-id "q-158012" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{3{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{3{y}^{2}} \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee68888-dbb2-5ca0-80cb-6c60f3bd0155" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290050} {:answer/id #uuid "8545cda7-dff1-5955-a591-94cf845e0016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290051} {:answer/id #uuid "56c46223-d9f3-5e31-ae79-b5c2146f681f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290052} {:answer/id #uuid "f20b16d2-b13d-5314-a9d2-801a551d4be7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290053} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb5bcff-df86-512b-b9bb-07304f9b353c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56c46223-d9f3-5e31-ae79-b5c2146f681f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290052} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcf3d22a-e0e4-5060-a63d-8decf4600d8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290049}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ca7be506-83fc-5b5f-8d5e-a2372dca466d" :question/math-academy-id "q-158014" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295244 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6ab1061-b24b-53f0-a11f-e4d8ef185175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={({x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295246} {:answer/id #uuid "09bbf700-f6cb-50e8-a453-bc5470a5818e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295247} {:answer/id #uuid "152a4131-f981-5e19-bc2b-581bd3c7a741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={({x}^{2/3}+K)}^{1/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295248} {:answer/id #uuid "98e72c92-6a3e-5cb9-93ca-61b6c716120a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{1/3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295249} {:answer/id #uuid "97acee09-353a-5f18-a0ce-d07def6bc92f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{1/2}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09bbf700-f6cb-50e8-a453-bc5470a5818e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295247} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d59afe4-4677-55e3-b49d-ea05d784509b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2fec0e0-010f-5a18-9431-739791e0738f" :question/math-academy-id "q-8304" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2} & =2{x}^{1/2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2}=2{x}^{1/2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2} & =2{x}^{1/2}+C \\\\ {y}^{3/2} & =3{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{3C}{2} \\\\ y & ={(3{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{3C}{2})}^{2/3} \\\\ y & ={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\frac{3C}{2}.$"}]}
